## Cypress Fixtures Overview

Fixtures are external data files that provide static test data for your Cypress tests. They help separate test data from test logic, making tests more maintainable and readable.

## Implementation Details

- Fixtures are stored in the `cypress/fixtures/` directory by default
- Support JSON, JS, and other file formats
- Can be loaded using `cy.fixture()` command
- Data is cached during test runs for performance

## Code Example

```javascript
// cypress/fixtures/user-data.json
{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com"
}

// cypress/component/UserComponent.spec.js
describe('UserComponent', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    cy.fixture('user-data').as('userData')
  })

  it('displays user information', function() {
    cy.mount(UserComponent, { props: { user: this.userData } })
    cy.get('[data-cy=user-name]').should('contain', 'John Doe')
  })
})
```

## Common Pitfalls

- Using `function() {}` instead of arrow functions to access fixture data via `this`
- Not properly handling async fixture loading
- Storing sensitive data in fixtures (use environment variables instead)

## Concept
Playwright provides user-centric locators that make tests more resilient to UI changes. getByRole() targets elements by their semantic meaning (button, link, etc.) while getByText() locates by visible text content.

## Implementation
```javascript
// getByRole - preferred for accessible testing
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).click();

// getByText - for text-based selection
await page.getByText('Welcome to dashboard').isVisible();

// Combining selectors
await page.getByRole('alert').getByText('Error occurred').isVisible();
```

## Trade-offs
**getByRole()**: More stable, accessibility-focused, but requires proper semantic HTML
**getByText()**: Direct but brittle to text changes, good for static content

## Pitfalls
- Avoid CSS selectors like $('.btn-primary') that break on style changes
- Use getByTestId() only when user-facing attributes aren't available
- getByRole() requires accessible markup to work effectively

